                <pb facs="0738" n="628" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg628"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ryan to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-02-10"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 10, 1890</date>.
                        (Received February 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 241.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to this legation’s dispatch No.
                    186 of December 11, 1889, relative to the arrest last November of Capt. J. H.
                    Stilphen, of the American schooner <hi rendition="#italic">Robert Ruff</hi>, by
                    the authorities of Minatitlan, Vera Cruz, I have the honor to inclose copies of
                    notes received by me from United States Consul Joseph D. Hoff, of Vera Cruz, and
                    from Capt. J. H. Stilphen.</p>
                <p>I have addressed a note to Mr. Mariscal, copy whereof please find herewith,
                    recalling his attention to this subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. Ryan.</hi></signed></closer>





